From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: EDEN_NX2_DEFER_RECORD and EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_REORDER take apart what a
 flush does

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series), a debug aid, off unless EDEN_NX2_DEFER_RECORD or
EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_REORDER is set. Not from upstream. Not for a release.

EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US=0 ended the white flashes in the Lost Woods (run178 to run180: 0 hot against
40 and 54 standing and 10 to 30 walking), at twice the submissions, and left few in Kokiri (run181,
run182: 1 each). Nobody knows which part of a flush does that. A
flush ends the render pass, resets the Z pass counter, drops command buffer state and with it raises
every dirty flag, closes the upload command buffer, and submits, which invalidates and flushes the
GPU caches and lets the fence land sooner. Both switches keep the 500 us window and its submission
count and add one part back.

EDEN_NX2_DEFER_RECORD=<mode>: whenever Scheduler::DeferFlush defers a flush, at any of its three
callers, it still does this much at that point:
1 InvalidateState only: dirty flags, bound pipeline.
2 Ends the render pass only.
3 Both.
4 As 3, and the Z pass counter reset: everything SubmitExecution records in the command buffer.
5 As 4, and a full barrier, ALL_COMMANDS to ALL_COMMANDS, memory write to memory read and write. It
  stands in for what a submission's start and end do to the caches, and it also orders execution.

Start with 5. Clean means the extra submissions are not needed, and the fix is in the recording or
in the caches at that point: then 4, then 3, 2 and 1 narrow it down. Still flashing means what is left
is the upload command buffer or the fence landing sooner.

EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_REORDER=1: CanReorderUpload says no, as the disable_buffer_reorder setting does,
which no env line reaches. An upload to a free region then stays in order among the draws instead of
moving to the start of the command buffer. It also ends the render pass at each upload, so read it
together with mode 2: clean here and flashing at 2 points to the reorder.

Cost: modes 2 to 5 add render pass ends, mode 5 also stops the GPU at each one. Mode 4 does what
window 0 does to the Z pass count, so it can drop samples like window 0. Unset, nothing changes. Not
built, not run.
---
 .../renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp       |  9 +++++-
 .../renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp          | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
index ffc1b47..d4d57c7 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
@@ -539,7 +539,14 @@ void BufferCacheRuntime::Finish() {
 
 bool BufferCacheRuntime::CanReorderUpload(const Buffer& buffer,
                                           std::span<const VideoCommon::BufferCopy> copies) {
-    if (Settings::values.disable_buffer_reorder) {
+    // EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_REORDER=1 (a debug aid): as the disable_buffer_reorder setting, which no
+    // env line reaches. An upload then stays in order among the draws, at the price of ending the
+    // render pass, instead of moving to the start of the command buffer.
+    static const bool no_reorder = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_REORDER");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    if (no_reorder || Settings::values.disable_buffer_reorder) {
         return false;
     }
     const bool can_use_upload_cmdbuf =
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
index 6dff4d9..3c40fa9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
@@ -175,6 +175,35 @@ bool Scheduler::DeferFlush() {
         std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - last_flush >= std::chrono::microseconds{interval_us}) {
         return false;
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_DEFER_RECORD=<mode> (a debug aid, unset or 0: off): a deferred flush still does to
+    // the recording what Flush does, so a test can tell that from the submission itself. 1 drops
+    // the command buffer state, 2 ends the render pass, 3 both, 4 also resets the Z pass counter,
+    // which is everything SubmitExecution records, and 5 adds a full barrier, which stands in for
+    // what a submission's start and end do to the GPU caches.
+    static const char record_mode = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_DEFER_RECORD");
+        return value != nullptr ? value[0] : '0';
+    }();
+    if (record_mode == '4' || record_mode == '5') {
+        EndPendingOperations();
+    } else if (record_mode == '2' || record_mode == '3') {
+        EndRenderPass();
+    }
+    if (record_mode == '1' || record_mode == '3' || record_mode == '4' || record_mode == '5') {
+        InvalidateState();
+    }
+    if (record_mode == '5') {
+        Record([](vk::CommandBuffer cmdbuf) {
+            static constexpr VkMemoryBarrier FULL_BARRIER{
+                .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_MEMORY_BARRIER,
+                .pNext = nullptr,
+                .srcAccessMask = VK_ACCESS_MEMORY_WRITE_BIT,
+                .dstAccessMask = VK_ACCESS_MEMORY_READ_BIT | VK_ACCESS_MEMORY_WRITE_BIT,
+            };
+            cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_ALL_COMMANDS_BIT,
+                                   VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_ALL_COMMANDS_BIT, 0, FULL_BARRIER);
+        });
+    }
     flush_pending = true;
     return true;
 }
